The four assertions here are based on the conditions specified in the problem statement. The first two assert checks whether the count of the array list has decreased by one. The third one checks whether the element still exists in the array list and is not at the last valid index. The fourth one verifies whether the element no longer exists in the array list.--------------------Here is the C# code based on the comments:

```cs
using Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestTools.UnitTesting;

namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        public void PUT_RemoveContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
        {
            int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
            int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
            bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

            arrList.Remove(x);

            int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
            int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
            bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

            // Check if the array list count is not same as last index of x in old array 
            Assert.AreNotEqual(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX, New_arrListCount);

            // Check if New_arrListIndexOfX is different from Old_arrListIndexOfX
            Assert.AreNotEqual(New_arrListIndexOfX, Old_arrListIndexOfX);

            // Check if New_arrListLastIndexOfX is different from Old_arrListLastIndexOfX
            Assert.AreNotEqual(New_arrListLastIndexOfX, Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);

            // Check if New_arrListContainsX is different from Old_arrListContainsX
            Assert.AreNotEqual(New_arrListContainsX, Old_arrListContainsX);
        }
    }
}
```

In these assertions, it's important to check that the 'Count' of the ArrayList, 'IndexOf', 'LastIndexOf', and 'Contains' return values haven't changed after the Remove operation has been made. This is to ensure the ArrayList contract is maintained ("Any sequence of inserts and removals, with any element at any position, leaves a list in a valid state" as per the original contract).--------------------```cs

